{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Machine-readable mirror of ai-conferences.md. That file is the human curation and explains why each source is here; this one is what tools/sync_catalog.py reads. Keep them in sync — tools/check_registry.py compares them.",
  "min_year": 2023,
  "fields": {
    "min_year": "The corpus floor: a talk known to be older than this is not derived into talks.json. 2023 is where this corpus changes subject — the modern-LLM vocabulary rate is 3-9% for 2015-2022 and 30% for 2023 — and no talk before it has a transcript. A conference or a source may override it, and null means no floor, which is how the security back catalogue is kept. A talk whose year is not known yet passes: the floor is a claim about talks proven old, and enrichment is what resolves a year. Enumeration still caches everything, so raising or lowering this is a re-derivation, not a re-fetch.",
    "scope": "'all' keeps every session (the conference is entirely about AI); 'ai' keeps only sessions whose title/description/tags match atu.AI_RE (general conferences with AI tracks).",
    "priority": "1 = fetch transcripts first. The caption endpoint is metered per IP, so the corpus is far bigger than any one sitting can transcribe; this is the rationing order.",
    "sources[].first": "Only page N entries deep into a channel before filtering. Channels list newest first, so this is a recency cap.",
    "sources[].year": "Set when a playlist is one edition, so the year filter works without per-video dates."
  },
